  },
  "TestCauseRace": {
   "class": "flaky",
   "reason": "flaky: Go 1.25.14's Cause reads the cause under the lock and then calls c.Err() when it is nil, so a cancel that lands between the two makes it return context.Canceled instead of the cause; the window is a few instructions in Go and wider in gocpp's unoptimized build (about 1 run in 300 fails); it can pass or fail"
  }
 },
